# Cabeçalhos de segurança do Netlify — valem nos DOIS sites (o dos clientes,
# publicado pelo GitHub, e o painel, publicado arrastando a pasta), porque a
# pasta public/ vai junto nos dois builds. O HSTS o Netlify já manda sozinho.
#
# Content-Security-Policy: o navegador só roda scripts do próprio site e só
# conversa com o Supabase deste projeto. Se um dia o projeto do Supabase
# mudar, troque o endereço em connect-src (https e wss).
# challenges.cloudflare.com = desafio anti-robô (Turnstile) do cadastro.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com; style-src 'self' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob:; connect-src 'self' https://iwekfmxrmmmxzjymtsyq.supabase.co wss://iwekfmxrmmmxzjymtsyq.supabase.co; manifest-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
